proposals.what:
Every Redo group header shows `≈ 20 pts at stake`, and a new header stat reads `Open mistakes: about 60 points at stake`. `progress.stake(learner, topic)` works it out as q × miss × slope, rounded to 5:
- q = the topic's questions per 44-question section (blueprint.DOMAIN_SPLIT's 35/35/15/15, split across a domain's topics by the same weights as the builder's `mix: blueprint`);
- miss = 1 − clean accuracy on the topic over the last 30 answers that are not repeats;
- slope = scaled Math points per raw question near the student's estimate (from scoring.ANCHORS at estimate.mean3, R16; 600 when there is no estimate).

It is shown only when the topic has at least 5 answers; otherwise the header reads `not enough answers yet`. An (i) popover gives the arithmetic in plain words: `About 3 Circles questions a test × you miss 45% × about 14 points each`. Group sort gains `Most points at stake`, which is the default when an estimate exists. After a Review session or a redo set, the summary shows the change for each topic touched: `Circles: at stake 20 → 10 pts`. /api/review/counts returns `stake_total` and each group returns `stake`.

When the pane opens a trap (`open=trap:<id>`), a horizontal timeline sits under the header. It has one dot per event from a new `trap_log(trap, at, event, session, seed)` table ('miss', 'repair', 'clean', 'fixed', 'check_ok', 'check_miss', 'relapse', 'dismissed'). Each dot has its glyph (✕ ↻ ✓), its date and a source chip, so the student can read the whole history, for example 'missed Sep 12 in practice, missed again Sep 15 in Section M1, clean Sep 18 and Sep 21, fixed, check-in passed Sep 24'. Tapping a dot opens that exact question.

Under the timeline is **Your rule**: a 120-character field (placeholder 'e.g. Subtract the given arc, don't halve'), saved on blur to traps.note (R9). It prompts with one line when hits ≥ 2 or after a relapse: 'Missed twice. Write the rule in your own words.' The rule comes back only after answering, never before:
- in the practice session's feedback when a miss opens or refreshes this trap, or any trap with the same norm on another template: `Your rule: …`;
- after a check-in is answered;
- on the traps sheet (proposal 11).

The rows show a note glyph when a rule exists.

The Saved tab opens with two cards, as on TopTierPrep's My Words: `Saved 14` and `Due today 4`. Each saved row gets a box (0–4) and a due date:
- saving sets due = tomorrow;
- a clean answer on a fresh version of its template moves it up a box, due in 1, 3, 7 and then 21 days;
- a miss sends it back to box 0, due tomorrow, and opens or refreshes the trap as usual;
- a clean answer in box 4 marks it `Learned`. It stays saved, is no longer due, and shows a check.

**Practise due · 4** serves one fresh version per due item. The row meta adds `due today` / `next Oct 2` / `Learned`, and the Status filter gains Due / Not due / Learned. Today's card and the queue in proposal 1 include saved items that are due. Settings adds `saved_spaced` (default on), so a student who only wants bookmarks can turn scheduling off.

'Again, exactly' and 'Fresh versions' on a History sitting header (and the report's retake) start the drill with `retake: sid` or `again: sid` (R10). The drill stores the parent sitting's id in its cfg. Its finish summary adds a **Then vs Now** block:
- two rows of result cells aligned by position (by template for fresh versions), with 'then' above 'now';
- a count of flips: `Fixed 3 · still wrong 1 · new miss 1 · right both times 7`;
- the score `9/12 → 11/12` and the time `14 min → 11 min`.

Clicking a column opens both questions in the pane side by side, then's pick against now's pick. In History, a sitting header gains `Retaken ×2 · best 11/12`, and its retakes nest under it, collapsed. Nothing is deleted. Exact retakes file as repeats (so mastery is honest), but the comparison still shows.

Between the stat strip and the tabs sits a 12-week chart (UI.barChart, stacked, with role=img and a hidden data table):
- graphite bars below the axis for mistakes opened, with the relapse part hatched;
- amber bars above for mistakes fixed;
- an ink line for the open count at the end of each week.

The legend carries counts. Hovering or tapping a week shows a tooltip `Sep 15–21 · 9 made · 12 fixed · open 28 → 25`; clicking opens Fixed or History for that week (since/until). A headline above the chart reads `This week: fixed 12, made 9, net −3` and `median days to fix 2 → 1.5 (last 4 weeks)`. One earned line appears only when fixed > made for the week: 'You're fixing them faster than you make them.' A phone shows 8 weeks and fits the width with no scroll. With under 2 weeks of data, the chart is replaced by a single line. Server: `GET /api/review/ledger?weeks=12` returns [{week, opened, relapsed, fixed, open_end}] from trap_log, in the X-Tz local week.
